# Project Architecture & Invariants

Two-domain system. Campaign servers (per language) drive donor traffic, multi-tenant store server processes payments. Routing is via signed token → store domain → store-side checkout-donor.ejs (cookie-authenticated) or checkout-store.ejs (cookie-less crawler / reviewer surface).

## Hard invariants — never violate

- Campaign servers never touch Stripe directly. All payments go through the store deployment.
- Donor session cookie is `httpOnly`. Token expiry is 5 minutes or less.
- Referrer-Policy is `strict-origin-when-cross-origin` globally. The ONLY `no-referrer` use is the meta-refresh HTML at `/s/:token` (breaks campaign→store referrer chain).
- Never log Stripe secret keys or include them in error messages.
- Never use `payment_method_types`. Always use `automatic_payment_methods: { enabled: true, allow_redirects: 'never' }`.
- Never use `?donated=true` or any donation-revealing query parameters. Use `?status=complete`.
- Never add micro-variance to decomposed line-item prices — Stripe drops all L2/L3 data when line sum ≠ total.
- Donor checkout (`checkout-donor.ejs`) MUST always use the campaign's color palette (`#00b964` / `#02a95c` / `#e8f8f0`), NEVER the store's own `store.colors`. The donor came from the campaign and expects visual continuity.

## Stripe metadata discipline (per PaymentIntent)

- `payment_details.order_reference` = reference code (required for L2/L3).
- `amount_details.tax.total_tax_amount` = 0 (required for L2/L3).
- `amount_details.line_items[]` = decomposed product items; exact sum must equal the PaymentIntent amount.
- Use store-specific metadata key names from `storeConfig.metadataKeys`. Each store MUST have unique key names — `store/scripts/sterility-check.js` is not the enforcement layer for this; the operator must hand-pick names per store.
- Update fulfillment evidence post-payment (`fulfillmentStatus = "delivered"`, `fulfilledAt = ISO timestamp`, `deliveryMethod = "digital_download"`).

## Stripe clustering defense (high-stakes)

Stripe's similarity clustering (2020), Payments Foundation Model (2025), and Fraudulent Website Signal (LLM, 2026 preview) detect cross-account links from:

- Shared bank account / email / IP / device fingerprint (operator hygiene).
- Identical product price tuples across accounts.
- Identical HTML/CSS template fingerprints across accounts.
- A single Apple Pay merchant-domain-association file served from multiple Stripe accounts.

Mitigations enforced in this repo:

- Per-store layout variants in `store/lib/layout-fingerprint.js` (one of 9 variants per store A–I, controls CSS variable names, nav class names, body class, header class, transition, font stack). Adding a new store REQUIRES adding a `VARIANTS` entry.
- Per-store price vectors generated with `store/scripts/generate-prices.js` (24 unique irregular prices per store, deterministic seed = store ID).
- Apple Pay file served ONLY via `APPLE_PAY_DOMAIN_ASSOCIATION` env var per deploy. The file is `.gitignored`. Never check in.
- `store/scripts/sterility-check.js` AND `campaign/scripts/sterility-check.js` both run at `prestart` and fail the boot on `gfm`/`cloaked`/`fundrais` literals (store side) / `gfm`/`cloaked` + `KNOWN_BAD_LITERALS` (campaign side). The campaign-side check is intentionally narrower because the campaign is donor-facing fundraising content where donor terminology is legitimate.

See `docs/CLUSTERING-AUDIT-2026-05.md` for the full audit and rationale.

## Database

- Supabase project: `wzialsfdguuircomaqvp` (`SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` in env).
- Use the Supabase MCP server for any schema-changing operation.
- Weighted store selection via `get_next_store()` RPC. `stores.weight_pct` (0-100); active weights should sum to 100. `status` is binary `active|paused`. Deficit-fill: the active store furthest below its target month-to-date share is picked.
- All money columns are decimal in the database. Stripe amounts are in cents (×100 at the boundary).

## Conventions

- No code comments unless they explain non-obvious intent/trade-offs.
- Campaign server port 3000, store server port 4000.
- Pull deeper context from `docs/`. AGENTS.md at root is the pointer map.
